# Line endings, normalised so a Windows checkout cannot change file contents.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. For this repo that is mostly harmless -- Python, YAML and
# Markdown all cope -- so this file is INSURANCE, not a fix for an observed
# failure. Saying so matters: the next person should not go hunting for the bug
# it prevented.
#
# Where it would stop being harmless:
#
#   - Anything under include/ that becomes a shell script. Astro bind-mounts
#     include/ into the Airflow container, so a CRLF script fails in Linux with
#     `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` -- an error that names the wrong problem.
#   - Checksums. The lab asserts byte-identical delivery data (D-022), and a
#     checkout that rewrites bytes would break that comparison for one platform
#     only, which is the worst kind of failure to reproduce.
#
# Astronomer documents no line-ending caveat for `astro dev start` (checked
# 2026-09-15: zero hits for CRLF or "line endings" in astro-cli). The Runtime
# image's own entrypoint ships inside the image and never touches the host
# checkout, so only files WE mount are exposed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly LF, because these cross into a Linux container.
*.py      text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.csv     text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.exe     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.gz      binary
*.zip     binary
*.sqlite3 binary
